      "question_text": "Neonatal jaundice: physiological jaundice appears?",
      "options": {
        "A": "At birth",
        "B": "After 24 hours (day 2-3)",
        "C": "After 7 days",
        "D": "At day 1"
      },
      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "Physiological jaundice: appears after 24 hours (day 2-3), peaks day 4-5, resolves by day 14 in term (21 in preterm). Pathological: appears <24h, bilirubin rising >5mg/dL/day, >12 mg/dL in term."
